<title>USA: European leaders firm on EMU deadline - Tarullo.</title>
<headline>European leaders firm on EMU deadline - Tarullo.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1997-06-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>European leaders were firm on their plans to undertake economic and monetary union (EMU) on its present schedule in their talks at the G7 annual summit, a senior U.S. official said on Saturday.</p>
<p>&quot;There was I think a fairly uniform view on the part of the European leaders that monetary integration would go forward on its present schedule,&quot; White House economic aide Dan Tarullo told reporters.</p>
<p>&quot;There was some mention of the additional measures to potentially increase employment which had been agreed to at Amsterdam,&quot; Tarullo added. &quot;The discussion really didn't get into the details of those to any considerable extent.&quot;</p>
<p>Tarullo was briefing reporters on discussions of the Group of Seven (G7) leading industrial nations -- Britain, Canada, France, Germany, Italy, Japan and the United Nations -- whose leaders met in Denver this weekend for their annual summit.</p>
